# Harness edit mode

Before changing harness structure, read `.cursor/shared/harness-principles.md`.

## Soft

- Clarify one module process; fix links/payload templates; add golden example; sync INDEX.
- Edit/add **role-specific** conventions inside **one** owning module (+ INDEX line); must/should present.
- Tighten wording without meaning change; sync module AGENTS link to conventions.

## Hard (ask human)

- Add/remove/rename module; change FSM/layers; move process out of `.cursor/`; fatten root AGENTS.
- Peer-handoff; weaken evidence/self-close; alwaysApply that loads all modules; duplicate canon into skills; second status SoR.
- Put conventions in `shared/` / overlays / repo root.
- Universal convention “for all roles”; copy/fork canon across modules (esp. security).
- Convention/constraints relay via OUTBOX; cross-read foreign `conventions/`.
- AlwaysApply on conventions; ship empty convention stubs without must/should.

## End checklist

- Principles read; placement ok; root still thin; INDEX updated.
- LIFECYCLE/ROUTING/contracts aligned; isolation ok.
- Convention file states who reads / who does not; process links to `conventions/INDEX`.
- No convention travel via contract; size budget ok.
- Note in `.cursor/shared/harness-changelog.md`.
